# 10. The 20-concept sequence is therefore important — but should be treated as a research queue

I agree with:

$$
Observation\rightarrow Dimension\rightarrow Statement\rightarrow Value\rightarrow Knowledge\rightarrow\cdots
$$

But I would change the interpretation slightly.

It is not yet proven that this is the **ontology's dependency order**.

It is:

$$
\boxed{
\text{current research dependency hypothesis}
}
$$

That distinction matters because research may discover that, for example:

$$
Evidence \prec Observation
$$

or that:

$$
Statement
$$

is not an independent object at all.

So every transition should be testable.

